      "description": "Who funds Congress: campaign contributions, outside spending and big donors for current members of Congress.",
      "generatedAt": "2026-11-17T00:31:57.741Z",
      "methodology": "Direct contributions from PACs and other political committees to current members of Congress, plus independent expenditures for and against them and the donors who gave an outside spender $50,000 or more in all, from FEC bulk data. Outside spending also counts 24/48-hour notices dated after a committee's last processed report, independent expenditures by groups and people that aren't political committees (Form 5), and, kept separate, electioneering communications (Form 9). Donor makeup splits individual money into small (unitemized) and itemized, and itemized money by the donor's state and, for House districts, ZIP code. Lobbyist bundling comes from campaigns' Form 3L reports. Each PAC is traced to the organization behind it (FEC connected organization, SEC EDGAR industry codes, lobbying disclosures, then keywords in the name) and given one of a fixed set of sectors. Contributor totals are counted by organization: an organization's PAC money plus itemized donations from people who list it as their employer. Lobbyists' former government jobs (covered positions on LD-1 and LD-2 filings) are matched to current members and committees by name, only when exactly one fits. Foreign agents come from FARA bulk data; their donations are itemized FEC contributions from people with a FARA short form in effect, matched by name and employer. Details: https://contributions.fyi/about/",
      "recordsComplete": true
    }
